1. Scope and official source

This license covers the original InfiniCrafterLocal source code, documentation,
project-owned assets and compiled distributions of the original project
(the "Project"), to the extent their respective copyright holders may license
them. The original project maintainer is Xipong (the "Maintainer").

The official source is https://github.com/Xipong/InfiniCrafterLocal, including
its Releases and GitHub-generated source archives. Another original-project
release channel is official only when the Maintainer explicitly designates it
in that repository. A third-party mirror or fork is not an official source.

This license is source-available, not an open-source license. It covers all
versions of the original Project, including earlier, current and future versions,
except material explicitly offered under separate terms. Publication of this
notice is not limited to version 0.4.254. It does not withdraw permissions already
validly granted under another license or individual written agreement.

2. Permitted use and development

Subject to this license, you may download, install, run and study the Project,
make private copies and backups, and modify and build it for your own use.
You may prepare and submit contributions to the official repository, including
through a working fork, branch or patch. You may share links to the official
source and official downloads, and publish reviews, gameplay videos, screenshots
and reasonable excerpts for discussion or documentation with attribution.
These permissions do not authorize independently distributing Project builds.

Nothing in this license limits rights already granted by GitHub's applicable
Terms of Service for public repositories, including viewing and creating copies
with GitHub's fork functionality. A GitHub working fork is not, by itself,
authorized to operate as an alternative product or release/download channel.

3. Original distributions: link to the official source

Except for the platform rights in section 2, the substantial-derivative
permission in section 4, or the Maintainer's explicit written permission,
you must not independently distribute or rehost the original Project, source
archives, compiled builds, installers or bundled copies. This prohibition
includes mirrors, alternative download pages, repacks, modpacks containing
Project files and renamed or cosmetically changed releases. Distribute links
to the official source instead. An attribution link alone does not authorize
a mirror or repack. There is no permission to sublicense the original Project
under different terms or remove its authorship, license or origin notices.

4. Substantial independent derivatives

You may independently distribute a derivative of the Project only if it has
Substantial Changes and all the conditions below are met. This is a specific
exception to section 3, not permission to mirror the original release.

"Substantial Changes" means implemented, demonstrable changes that give the
derivative materially different functionality, architecture or user workflow
from the identified upstream version. Examples include a major new subsystem,
a genuinely different generation/runtime workflow, or a substantive systemic
rework. Assess the result as a whole, not its line count or claimed effort.

Renaming, changing a logo or colors, a version bump, translating text, editing
default settings, dependency updates, repackaging, isolated minor fixes, or
combining such changes without materially different functionality do not,
by themselves, qualify. Mere assertions of substantial changes do not qualify.

A distributed substantial derivative must:
(a) use a distinct product name and clearly state that it is an unofficial
    derivative, not an official InfiniCrafterLocal release;
(b) identify the upstream version or commit and prominently link to the official
    source in its repository, primary download page and accompanying README;
(c) describe its Substantial Changes concretely in a changelog or comparison;
(d) preserve applicable authorship, attribution and this license, including in
    source archives and accompanying binary-distribution materials;
(e) provide the corresponding modified Project source, including build scripts
    and dependency manifests needed to build the distributed version, under
    this license, at no additional charge; external dependencies remain subject
    to their own licenses and need not be bundled;
(f) not imply endorsement by the Maintainer or present upstream work as its own;
(g) not offer unmodified or merely cosmetic original-project builds as a separate
    download under cover of the substantial derivative.

If your changes do not satisfy this section, submit a pull request or seek
explicit written permission before publishing an independent distribution.
A derivative permitted by this section is still subject to this license; its
recipients do not obtain unrestricted rights to redistribute the original.

5. Contributions and permissions

Pull requests to the official repository are the preferred way to improve the
Project. Preference for PRs is not an obligation to submit private changes, a
promise of acceptance, or a requirement to obtain approval for a derivative
that already satisfies section 4.

By intentionally submitting a contribution for inclusion, you confirm that you
may license that contribution under these terms, unless a separate agreement
says otherwise. You retain your authorship; submission does not assign ownership.
Third-party material must be identified with its original license and notices.

Requests for exceptions may be made through an issue or discussion in the
official repository, addressed to Xipong. An exception must be explicitly granted
in writing by the Maintainer; silence, an open issue or a pending PR is not consent.

